Remaining items from the code & test review (2026-08-17)
https://claude.ai/code/artifact/c24a279f-b66e-4b6f-ab0a-a7c8ba2df0d8

DONE so far: C1-C8 (all correctness defects) - see git log e123fd0..b2e1d57
STILL OPEN: the server lifecycle (L), missing capabilities (M) and test (T) items below.

Suggested order from the review: T2 + T5 first (CI + corpus test, makes everything
after it verifiable), then L1, then T1 + L2-L4, then M1.

NOTE on the corpus/T5 idea: "assert zero errors on files that compile standalone"
is weaker than it sounds - 64tass skips unreferenced .proc bodies, so a file that is
one big .proc passes trivially while validating nothing. A real corpus test must
reference the procs or assemble each file through its actual parent.

optional: case-insensitive labels

-----------------------

SERVER LIFECYCLE (all in server.ts, which has no tests)

L1 (High) - configuration changes never reach the server
	connection.onDidChangeConfiguration cannot fire: vscode-languageclient only
	sends workspace/didChangeConfiguration if the client sets
	synchronize.configurationSection or the server dynamically registers for it,
	and we do neither (clientOptions.synchronize is {} in extension.ts).
	So changing 64tass.caseSensitive does nothing until the window is reloaded -
	contradicting the CHANGELOG's "Index automatically rebuilds when setting changes".
	fix: register DidChangeConfigurationNotification.type in onInitialized when
	hasConfigurationCapability. While there: that handler also needs to clear include
	refs and re-publish diagnostics for open documents - today it re-indexes but
	leaves stale diagnostics on screen.

L2 (Medium) - closing an included file drops it from the index
	onDidClose calls documentIndex.delete(uri) unconditionally. If that file is
	.include'd by a still-open document, the parent loses every symbol it provided.
	includeRefCount already holds what's needed to decide this.
	fix: only delete when no other root still references the URI.

L3 (Medium) - re-indexing reads includes from disk, discarding unsaved buffers
	indexDocument always fs.readFileSync's an included file even when it is open with
	unsaved edits, so editing the parent silently reverts the include's index.
	fix: reuse getDocumentText (server.ts), which already checks the open buffer first.

L4 (Medium) - diagnostics published only for the document that changed
	Editing an include never refreshes the parent's diagnostics. No
	didChangeWatchedFiles registration either, so edits made outside the editor are
	invisible.
	fix: revalidate the include graph the changed document participates in; register
	a file watcher for the handled extensions.

L5 (Low) - no workspace scan on startup
	Only open documents and their include trees are indexed, so go-to-definition and
	find-references silently return nothing for symbols in unopened files, with no
	signal distinguishing "not found" from "not looked at".
	This is the main remaining source of "Undefined symbol" noise in the corpus.
	fix: scan workspace folders for the handled extensions on initialize.

-----------------------

DESIGN CALL - symbols in inactive .if branches: DECIDED & DONE
	Chose option B (evaluate constant conditions, suppress only provably-dead
	branches) plus a "; 64tass-langserv: define NAME = VALUE" pragma emulating
	64tass's -D flag, so build-time flags can be resolved too.
	Corpus effect: undefined-symbol warnings 559 -> 538.
	Note ~36 of the remaining conditional warnings are undecidable only because the
	flag lives in a file we never indexed - fixing L5 (or adding a define pragma)
	is what unlocks those, not more evaluator work.

-----------------------

MISSING CAPABILITIES (ordered by value/effort; first three are nearly free)

M1 - documentSymbol. No outline, no breadcrumbs, no Ctrl+Shift+O. DocumentIndex.labels
     already carries name, kind, range and scope path - it is a mapping function.
M2 - workspaceSymbol (Ctrl+T). Blocked on L5 being useful.
M3 - prepareRename. DONE as part of the C8 fix (bfa4fd8).
M4 - signatureHelp for macro/function calls; parametersAtScope is already populated.
M5 - definition on .binclude / .binary paths (onDefinition handles .include only,
     while completions.ts already covers all three).
M6 - documentHighlight (occurrences of the symbol under the cursor).
M7 - semantic tokens, to disambiguate what the TextMate grammar cannot.
M8 - no debounce on validation: every keystroke re-indexes the whole include tree
     and runs a full validation pass.

-----------------------

TEST SUITE

T1  - server.ts has zero tests, and 5 of the 13 defects lived there. computeFoldingRanges
      in particular should move to its own module so folding is testable at all
      (the C6 fix touched the folding path and could NOT be covered by a test).
T2  - nothing runs the tests in CI. release.yml fires only on v* tags and never
      invokes yarn test or yarn typecheck. Highest-value single addition.
T3  - the release workflow runs npm install against a yarn.lock, so the lockfile is
      ignored. Either commit package-lock.json or use yarn install --frozen-lockfile.
T4  - integration tests vanish silently off this machine: TASS_PATH is hardcoded to
      /home/db/bin/64tass and describe.skipIf turns its absence into a green run.
      Make it env-overridable and hard-fail under a REQUIRE_TASS flag.
T5  - no false-positive corpus test (see the NOTE at the top about why the obvious
      version of this is misleading).
T6  - case sensitivity is never verified against the compiler; compile() takes
      extraFlags but -C is never passed anywhere.
T7  - buildIndex() cannot build a mixed-sensitivity index: it reads caseSensitive from
      args[0] and applies it to every document (test/helpers/doc.ts), so the
      per-document pragma cascade cannot be tested across documents.
T8  - rename tests do not cover renaming across files, the comment-edit annotation
      path (needsConfirmation), or rejection of invalid identifiers.
T9  - no assertions on diagnostic ranges in most tests. operandStart is computed with
      code.indexOf(operand), which finds the first occurrence, not the operand's
      actual position - an off-by-column risk.
T10 - performance.test.ts is a benchmark in the unit directory, running and appending
      to performance-results.jsonl on every yarn test. (Left as-is deliberately.)
T11 - no coverage tooling (@vitest/coverage-v8 not installed).
T12 - yarn lint is broken: the script is declared but ESLint is not a dependency and
      no config file exists, so it exits 2.

-----------------------

DOCS & HYGIENE

D1 - completions are undocumented: directive, opcode, symbol, parameter and file-path
     completion ship in completions.ts but appear in neither README nor CHANGELOG.
D2 - CHANGELOG stops at 0.8.0 while package.json reads 0.8.2. Nothing since is
     documented anywhere a user would look (case-sensitivity pragma, completions,
     and the whole C1-C8 series).
D3 - the CHANGELOG states something untrue: "Index automatically rebuilds when setting
     changes" (0.8.0). Per L1 it does not.
D4 - tsconfig.json includes only src/**/*, so yarn typecheck never type-checks the
     test suite; vitest transpiles without checking, so type errors in tests go unnoticed.
